DD target line extension memo

- Goal: When the canvas depth scale is drilling_depth and Finder has a clicked target, show target lines not only on the clicked section, but also on sections that correspond to the same composite_depth.
- Current behavior: DD target line is limited to the clicked hole/section because drilling_depth is local and the same DD value is not comparable across sections.
- Proposed display-only approach:
  - Keep the canvas axis as drilling_depth.
  - Use finderData.composite_depth as the shared reference depth.
  - For each visible section, check whether the section contains that composite_depth between adjacent markers.
  - If contained, interpolate the corresponding drilling_depth in that section.
  - Draw the Finder target line at that interpolated drilling_depth.
- Scope:
  - Prefer renderer/js/renderer.js only.
  - No core logic change should be needed.
- Helper idea:
  - Add a small renderer-side interpolation helper such as interpolateSectionDepth(section, sourceField, targetField, sourceValue).
  - For this feature, sourceField is composite_depth and targetField is drilling_depth.
- Safety:
  - Do not extrapolate at first. Draw only when the composite_depth is inside a marker interval.
  - Skip intervals with null composite_depth or null drilling_depth.
  - Multiple matching sections may draw multiple target lines; this is acceptable initially and can be narrowed later if needed.
- Estimated cost:
  - Implementation: 30-60 minutes.
  - Manual verification: 20-30 minutes.
  - Risk: low to medium, if kept as display-only renderer logic.
